# Bismuth (R -3 m, number 166) on hexagonal axes: the crystal of
# bi_rh_number_only.cif (a_h = 2 a_r sin(alpha/2), c_h = a_r sqrt(3)
# sqrt(1 + 2 cos alpha)). Fixture for test_cif_reader_symmetry.cpp: the
# space group is given only by its number, and the cell (alpha = 90,
# gamma = 120 deg) is the hexagonal one, so the setting is R -3 m:H and Bi
# on 6c (0,0,z) gives 6 atoms: (0,0,+-z) with the R-centring translations
# (2/3,1/3,1/3) and (1/3,2/3,2/3).
